cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "rankin-selberg-delta: the Rankin-Selberg method for level-one cusp forms in Lean 4, from the modular discriminant to the explicit formula of L(Delta x Delta-bar)"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalisation, built on Mathlib, of the Rankin-Selberg method for level-one cusp forms and
  its consequences for the modular discriminant Delta. (1) The Rankin-Selberg Dirichlet series
  D(w) = sum |a(n)|^2 n^{-w} of a nonzero level-one cusp form has a simple pole with positive residue,
  through real-analytic Eisenstein series and unfolding; and L(Delta, 1 + it) is nonzero for real t != 0.
  (2) A de la Vallee Poussin zero-free region for the Rankin-Selberg square
  G(s) = zeta(2s) D(s + 11) of Delta. (3) The Weil explicit formula for G, for smooth compactly
  supported test functions, with the zero count N_G(T) = O(T log T). Every theorem depends only on
  the standard axioms. Unrefereed; produced autonomously by AI agents running inside a custom research harness.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nozero Day"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - Rankin-Selberg method
  - modular discriminant
  - Ramanujan tau function
